    {
      "ancestors": [],
      "attributes": [
        {
          "doc_text": " Signals a memory allocation error.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            19188,
            19226
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            19227,
            19230
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " Callers of memory allocation APIs wishing to cease execution",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            19231,
            19295
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " in response to an allocation error are encouraged to call this function,",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            19296,
            19372
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " rather than directly invoking [`panic!`] or similar.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            19373,
            19429
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            19430,
            19433
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " This function is guaranteed to diverge (not return normally with a value), but depending on",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            19434,
            19529
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " global configuration, it may either panic (resulting in unwinding or aborting as per",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            19530,
            19618
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " configuration for all panics), or abort the process (with no unwinding).",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            19619,
            19695
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            19696,
            19699
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " The default behavior is:",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            19700,
            19728
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            19729,
            19732
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "  * If the binary links against `std` (typically the case), then",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            19733,
            19800
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "   print a message to standard error and abort the process.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            19801,
            19863
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "   This behavior can be replaced with [`set_alloc_error_hook`] and [`take_alloc_error_hook`].",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            19864,
            19960
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "   Future versions of Rust may panic by default instead.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            19961,
            20020
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            20021,
            20024
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " * If the binary does not link against `std` (all of its crates are marked",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            20025,
            20102
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "   [`#![no_std]`][no_std]), then call [`panic!`] with a message.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            20103,
            20170
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "   [The panic handler] applies as to any panic.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            20171,
            20221
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            20222,
            20225
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " [`set_alloc_error_hook`]: ../../std/alloc/fn.set_alloc_error_hook.html",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            20226,
            20300
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " [`take_alloc_error_hook`]: ../../std/alloc/fn.take_alloc_error_hook.html",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            20301,
            20377
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " [The panic handler]: https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/runtime.html#the-panic_handler-attribute",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            20378,
            20479
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " [no_std]: https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/names/preludes.html#the-no_std-attribute",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            20480,
            20570
          ],
